# Resolution: Engine inspection, search hardening, full docs, npm/CI-CD open-source publishing kit

## Validation Checklist
- [x] Verify cargo test --workspace passes (baseline and after search changes) — all suites green, incl. golden perft, searcher-unification golden, regression, rules-integration
- [x] Verify cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings is clean (required fixing pre-existing eq_op error in hyperchess-driver)
- [x] Verify cargo fmt --all --check is clean (required [workspace] table in excluded CUDA crate for worktree checkouts)
- [x] Verify pnpm install/build/test pass — BUILD_OK; 70 tests green (core 44, store 12, board 8, theme 6); required fixing pre-existing ProSearcher wasm32 compile break
- [x] Verify no secrets (GitLab PAT, tokens) in any committed file — tree scan and full-history scan (25 commits): 0 hits
- [x] Verify hyperchess-search-cuda still has publish = false
- [x] Verify draft PR opened on GitHub (hyperchessdev account), branch only — no changes pushed to main
- [x] Verify release workflows default to dry-run (no accidental publish) — both release-npm.yml and release-crates.yml default dry_run=true and refuse to publish without secrets

## Outcomes / Summary

### Engine inspection (vs the HyperChess laws)
The engine implements the full law set: 12×12 board, Eagle/Hawk jumpers (movegen + SEE values +
unblockable-check handling), rank-3/10 double-step + en passant, rank-12/1 promotion incl. E/H,
g-file castling, 224-half-move rule, raptor insufficient material. The search stack was already
unified on the canonical TimedSearcher; verified by the searcher_unification_golden test.

### Search hardening (new, unique)
1. Countermove refutation table (144×144, butterfly-indexed by the opponent's previous move),
   ordered in a strict band between killers (7500) and quiet history (≤6900).
2. "Raptor bonus" — HyperChess-specific ordering: quiet Eagle/Hawk moves landing within
   Chebyshev ≤ 4 of the enemy king (their jump range) get +400 inside the quiet band, because
   raptor checks cannot be blocked by interposition. 5 new unit tests pin the ordering bands.

### Pre-existing breakages found and fixed
- hyperchess-wasm did not compile for wasm32 (leftover ProSearcher import + duplicated
  "strategic" match arm from the profile-rename commit) — the WASM SDK was unbuildable on main.
- hyperchess-driver failed clippy -D warnings (eq_op: duplicated "strategic" comparison;
  duplicated match literal).
- cargo fmt/metadata failed from git worktrees (excluded CUDA crate lacked a [workspace] table).

### Publishing kit
- Docs: rewritten root README (laws table, npm/Rust/WASM quickstarts vs verified APIs, GPL
  boundary guidance), docs/search-architecture.md (full technique + safety-invariant +
  tuning reference), docs/hyperchess-laws.md, package READMEs for board/store/theme.
- Community: CONTRIBUTING, CODE_OF_CONDUCT (Covenant 2.1), SECURITY (private reporting,
  scope), ACKNOWLEDGMENTS (Stockfish, CPW, MCTS/UCT literature, toolchains), CITATION.cff,
  CHANGELOG, issue templates (bug/feature/config), PR template.
- npm: unified GPL-3.0-or-later across all 5 packages; repository/homepage/bugs/keywords/
  publishConfig/engines metadata added.
- crates.io: workspace repository/homepage → GitHub; per-crate readme/keywords/categories;
  version keys on path deps (publish order eval→rules→search→wasm; driver excluded while its
  optional cuda feature references the unpublished CUDA crate).
- CI/CD: ci.yml extended (wasm32 check job; js job builds real WASM), security.yml
  (cargo-audit + pnpm audit, weekly + manifest-change triggered), release-crates.yml +
  release-npm.yml (manual, dry-run default, token-gated), dependabot.yml.
